# .dockerignore -- shrinks the build context sent to the daemon and keeps the
# builder-stage `COPY . .` layer from being invalidated by edits to files that
# have nothing to do with compiling the binary.
#
# ############################################################################
# READ THIS BEFORE "TIDYING UP" THIS FILE -- two go:embed landmines
# ############################################################################
#
#   1. main.go                    contains //go:embed CHANGELOG.md
#   2. internal/storage/migrate.go contains //go:embed migrations/*.sql
#
# Consequences:
#   * NEVER add a blanket `*.md` / `**/*.md` rule without the
#     `!CHANGELOG.md` negation below -- the build dies with
#     `pattern CHANGELOG.md: no matching files found`.
#   * NEVER exclude `*.sql` or `**/*.sql`. The migrations are embedded into
#     the binary. `queries.sql` (a docs-only sample-query file) is therefore
#     excluded by its exact path, never by a glob.
#
# This is an explicit denylist rather than an allowlist precisely because of
# those two embeds: a `*` + `!keep-me` allowlist is far easier to get subtly
# wrong here.
# ############################################################################

# --- VCS / agent metadata --------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.claude

# --- Editor & OS junk ------------------------------------------------------
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Secrets & local configuration -----------------------------------------
# config.toml / .env are gitignored but may exist on a developer machine and
# would otherwise be baked into the build context with real credentials.
# The *.example templates are excluded too: they are documentation, and
# nothing in the Go build reads them.
config.toml
config.toml.example
.env
*.env
.env.example
.envrc

# --- Documentation ---------------------------------------------------------
# `**/*.md` also catches the per-package CLAUDE.md files under cmd/ and
# internal/. The negation right after it is MANDATORY -- see the header.
docs
**/*.md
!CHANGELOG.md

# Sample queries for humans. Exact path on purpose: a `*.sql` glob would
# strip internal/storage/migrations/*.sql and break the embed.
queries.sql

# --- Dev tooling (not compiled) --------------------------------------------
Taskfile.yml
Taskfile.local.yml
Makefile
mise.toml
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.golangci.yml
.yamllint.yml
.markdownlint.yml
.markdownlintignore
.codespellrc
.air.toml
.actrc

# --- Scripts ---------------------------------------------------------------
*.sh

# --- Build outputs & test artifacts ----------------------------------------
rmm-tracker
tmp
.task
*.test
*.out
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.dump.sql

# --- Docker's own files ----------------------------------------------------
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.*
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
.dockerignore
